From 4ce6f18db19a09833eba6cf75fa496a8b358e7ef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 16:55:37 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(viabedrock): retain Bedrock creative catalog entries

Preserve creative groups and exact entry identities so client UI can reflect the connected Bedrock server catalog and duplicate Java fallback items still resolve to the intended Bedrock item. Resync creative slot contents after sending transactions to avoid local ghost items reported by testers.

Request creative stacks through CraftCreative palette IDs, CraftResults,
optional Destroy, and Place actions. Reconcile their authoritative network
IDs before processing queued selections. Preserve queued creative writes
when Java closes its local GUI, while discarding screen-specific clicks.
Use the same container request-slot boundary for armor and offhand slots.

The request sequence matches protocol 2193 and Geyser 2.11.3 build 1247
PlayerInventoryTranslator.translateCreativeRequest. Unit tests check
palette identity, replacement/deletion, equipment destinations, and
acknowledgment ordering across GUI close. No Geyser changes are required.

Open the native player inventory before sending creative requests and wait for its acknowledgement. Preserve writes across delayed OPEN responses and local Java GUI closure. Writes arriving during a pending native CLOSE remain queued and reopen the inventory after the acknowledgement, rather than disappearing between native windows. Packet-handler tests cover rapid writes with distinct slots and quantities during that close.

Retain exact creative entry identity and complete native item snapshots; reject ambiguous same-Java-item fallbacks rather than choosing arbitrary potion/custom variants. Enforce the native creative stack maximum. Catalog and transfer tests cover exact markers, component differences and oversized selections.

Translate Java creative-menu drops from slot -1 into native creative
craft/results/drop actions without replacing held inventory. Java 26.3
bytecode emits this slot for creative-menu Q. Geyser
PlayerInventoryTranslator documents the same native created-output slot
50 flow since Bedrock 1.18.2. Actual packet tests cover plate and stone
counts, pending-close queuing, and invalid stack bounds.
